Subtask 1.2: Create HTTP Fault Injection Policy
Now we'll create fault injection policies to simulate various failure scenarios.

Create a fault injection configuration for HTTP delays:
cat > http-delay-fault.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: reviews-delay-fault
  namespace: bookinfo
spec:
  hosts:
  - reviews
  http:
  - match:
    - headers:
        end-user:
          exact: jason
    fault:
      delay:
        percentage:
          value: 100.0
        fixedDelay: 7s
    route:
    - destination:
        host: reviews
        subset: v2
  - route:
    - destination:
        host: reviews
        subset: v1
EOF
Apply the delay fault injection:
kubectl apply -f http-delay-fault.yaml
Create destination rules for traffic routing:
cat > reviews-destination-rule.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: DestinationRule
metadata:
  name: reviews
  namespace: bookinfo
spec:
  host: reviews
  subsets:
  - name: v1
    labels:
      version: v1
  - name: v2
    labels:
      version: v2
  - name: v3
    labels:
      version: v3
EOF
kubectl apply -f reviews-destination-rule.yaml
