Task 2: Simulate Network Latency and Request Failures
Subtask 2.1: Test Delay Fault Injection
Get the gateway URL:
export INGRESS_HOST=$(kubectl -n istio-system get service istio-ingressgateway -o jsonpath='{.status.loadBalancer.ingress[0].ip}')
export INGRESS_PORT=$(kubectl -n istio-system get service istio-ingressgateway -o jsonpath='{.spec.ports[?(@.name=="http2")].port}')
export GATEWAY_URL=$INGRESS_HOST:$INGRESS_PORT

echo "Gateway URL: http://$GATEWAY_URL"
Test normal request without fault injection:
# Test normal request
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "Time: %{time_total}s, Status: %{http_code}\n" \
  "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage"
Test request with delay fault injection:
# Test with jason user (should experience delay)
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "Time: %{time_total}s, Status: %{http_code}\n" \
  -H "Cookie: user=jason" \
  "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage"
Create a script to continuously test delay injection:
cat > test-delay.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
echo "Testing delay fault injection..."
for i in {1..5}; do
  echo "Request $i:"
  echo -n "  Normal user: "
  curl -s -o /dev/null -w "Time: %{time_total}s, Status: %{http_code}\n" \
    "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage"
  
  echo -n "  Jason user: "
  curl -s -o /dev/null -w "Time: %{time_total}s, Status: %{http_code}\n" \
    -H "Cookie: user=jason" \
    "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage"
  echo "---"
  sleep 2
done
EOF

chmod +x test-delay.sh
./test-delay.sh
